*
*	MULTOS/8 ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS:
*
*
*	FIRST, EDIT THE PARAM FILE AND SET ALL PARAMETERS. GENERALLY,
*		IF AN OPTION IS DESIRED, ITS PARAMETER IS SET TO 1.
*
*	THEN, ASSEMBLE 'JOBS' WITH PAGE8 AS FOLLOWS:
*
*	.R PAGE8
*	*JOBS<PARAM,JOBS
*
*	THIS PRODUCES THE 'JOBS.BN' FILE WHICH YOU MUST USE WITH BUILD.SV
*	TO CREATE A HANDLER FOR ALL THE TERMINALS (JOBS) IN YOUR SYSTEM.
*	BE SURE TO RUN BUILD.SV WITH THE 'JOBS' HANDLER BEFORE TRYING
*	TO RUN MULTOS THE FIRST TIME. ALSO, DELETE THE 'RKB0' HANDLER
*	IF IT IS CURRENTLY IN YOUR SYSTEM. THE SYSTEM DEVICES FOR THE
*	TERMINALS (JOBS) IN YOUR SYSTEM REQUIRE =ALL= THE SPACE ON
*	RK05 DRIVE 0.
*
*	THEN, ASSEMBLE 'MULTOS' WITH PAGE8 AS FOLLOWS:
*
*	.R PAGE8
*	*MULTOS,DEV:MULTOS<PARAM,OSA,OSB,OSC,OSD
*
*	BE SURE TO MAKE THE THIRD PASS LISTING FILE GO TO A DEVICE OTHER
*	THAN 'SYS:' IF YOU DESIRE THE LISTING. (SEE THE PAGE8 MANUAL FOR
*	DETAILS.)
*
	PAGE	77		Set page depth
	TITLE	Parameters for assembly of MULTOS/8
*
	NOTE:	(Customer Name)
	NOTE:	---------------
*
PDP8E	EQU	1		0=PDP8/I,L; 1=PDP-8/A,E,F,M
*
*********************************************************
RK8E	EQU	1		DON'T CHANGE THESE	*
RK8L	EQU	2					*
RL01	EQU	3					*
PERTEC	EQU	5					*
*********************************************************
*
SYS:DISK EQU	RK8E		SET TO RK8E (SUPPORT FOR RK8L, RL01 IS NOT IN)
*
RKO5	EQU	1		0=ONLY 1 RK05 DRIVE; 1=MORE THAN 1 RK05 DRIVE
*
DECTAPE	EQU	0		0=NO DECTAPE; 1=TC08 OR TD8E DECTAPE
*
TC08	EQU	0		0=NO TC08 DECTAPE; 1=TC08 DECTAPE (NOT YET)
*
TD8E	EQU	0		0=NO TD8E DECTAPE; 1=TD8E DECTAPE
*
MAGTAPE	EQU	0		0=NO MAGTAPE; 1=TM8E MAGTAPE
*
V132	EQU	0		1=DATA PRINTER MODEL V132
*
UPCHAR	EQU	0		POWER UP PRINTER ENABLE CHARACTER
*
*	THE FOLLOWING 3 PARAMETERS ARE NOT USED IF YOUR PRINTER DOES NOT
*	REQUIRE 'FILLER' CHARACTERS AFTER A LINE OR FORM FEED.
*
FFNPL	EQU	0		PRINTER NULLS PER LINE AFTER A FORM FEED
LFNUL	EQU	0		PRINTER NULLS AFTER A LINE FEED
*
*	If you printer is being driven on a CRT interface and the keyboard
*	flag has any possibility of ever being set, set the following
*	parameter to the clear keyboard flag IOT.
*
PRKEY	EQU	0		CLEAR PRINTER KEYBOARD FLAG
*
*	SET THE FOLLOWING PARAMETER TO 1 IF YOU HAVE ANY KL8E INTERFACES
*	IN YOUR SYSTEM. IT IS NOT NEEDED IF ALL YOUR INTERFACES ARE KL8JA'S.
*
KL8E	EQU	1		0=KL8-JA INTERFACES; 1=KL8E
TERMS	EQU	3		2, 3, OR 4
TERM2	EQU	40		TTY # 2 KEYBOARD DEVICE CODE
TERM3	EQU	30		TTY # 3 KEYBOARD DEVICE CODE
TERM4	EQU	0		TTY # 4 KEYBOARD DEVICE CODE
*
*	KL8A SUPPORT HAS NOT YET BEEN ADDED.
*
KL8A	EQU	0		0=NO KL8-A; OTHERWISE, DEVICE CODE
*
PTR	EQU	0		1=PR8-E PAPER TAPE READER; 0=NONE
PTP	EQU	0		1=PP8E PAPER TAPE PUNCH; 0=NONE
*
FLOPPY	EQU	0		1=RX8-E FLOPPY; 0=NONE
*
*	LINE FREQUENCY MUST BE SPECIFIED IF YOU HAVE A LINE FREQUENCY CLOCK.
*
HERTZ	EQU	0		CLOCK FREQUENCY (50 OR 60)
DK8EA	EQU	0		1=LINE FREQ REAL TIME CLOCK
DK8EC	EQU	0		1=CRYSTAL
DK8EP	EQU	0		1=PROGRAMMABLE
DKC8AA	EQU	1		1=PDP-8/A CRYSTAL
*
EAE	EQU	0		1=KE8-E EAE; 0=NO EAE
*
SPOOL	EQU	1		0=NO PRINT SPOOLING; 1=SPOOLING
*
*	MAKE NO CHANGES TO THE FOLLOWING DEFINITIONS:
*
JOBS	EQU	TERMS+SPOOL
